  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Human Rights Advocacy Centre/Eastern Europe</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">European Human Rights Advocacy Centre/&#xD6;steuropa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Through expert legal support, lawyers and human rights defenders have
increased skills, capacity and resilience to challenge human rights abuses.
2. Through trauma-informed litigation, applicants voices are heard and barriers
to justice challenged, leading to increased access to justice for vulnerable and
persecuted communities.
3. Through litigation, national and international precedents are set, leading to
increased national protection and raised international human rights standards
across the region.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Med denna insats, &quot;Fighting for human rights in times of war and repression, 2024-2027, ska European Human Rights Advocacy Centre (EHRAC) arbeta med m&#xE4;nniskor&#xE4;ttsf&#xF6;rsvarare i Ukraina, Georgien, Azerbajdzjan och Armenien.
Bidraget kommer att st&#xE4;rka demokrati, m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter och j&#xE4;mst&#xE4;lldhet i regionen. EHRAC fokuserar strategiska internationella MR-instrument och mekanismer f&#xF6;r att genom r&#xE4;ttstvister st&#xE4;rka m&#xE4;nskliga r&#xE4;ttigheter och r&#xE4;ttsstatsprincipen i samarbete med lokala civilsamh&#xE4;llesorganisationer.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With this project, &quot;Fighting for human rights in times of war and repression&quot;, 2024-2027 submitted initially to Sida 2023-11-30, European Human Rights Advocacy Centre (EHRAC) proposes to work with human rights defenders (HRDs) across Ukraine, Georgia, Azerbaijan and Armenia, take on strategic legal challenges and aims hold governments to account through the use of international humanitarian and human rights law and connected mechanisms.
The contribution will enhance democracy and gender equality at a pivotal time
for the region.</narrative>
  </description>
